nt). Manual escape hatch alongside the autopilot purge phase.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"older_than_hours\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Age cutoff in hours. Default 72.\"},\"yes\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Consent to the irreversible brain-wide purge. Ask the user first.\"}},\"required\":[]},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":false}},{\"name\":\"fetch\",\"description\":\"Fetch the full text of one search result by its opaque, source-qualified `id` (OpenAI deep-research contract: the search/fetch pair). Pass the id unchanged; it does not grant access. Legacy slug ids work only when unambiguous within your current read scope. Returns { id, title, text, url, metadata } — `text` is the page's canonical markdown; a page over 256 KB returns the window around the searched chunk instead, with metadata.total_bytes and metadata.next_id (fetch it to read on). For fuzzy slugs, soft-delete recovery, or lossless edit round-trips, use get_page.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Opaque result id from a prior `search` call. Pass unchanged. Unambiguous legacy slugs are also accepted.\"},\"include_quarantined\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Admin: quarantined body.\"},\"min_trust\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Lowest trust tier to return (the connection floor still applies).\",\"enum\":[\"user_confirmed\",\"operator_curated\",\"tool_observed\",\"agent_written\",\"unknown\",\"external_untrusted\"]}},\"required\":[\"id\"]},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":true}},{\"name\":\"find_pages\",\"description\":\"Find pages by name or path (what ls/find would answer), sorted by slug. pattern: a glob ('people/*acme*') matched against slug or source path, a slug prefix ('companies/acme'), or a plain name ('acme', a case-insensitive substring of the title or the slug's last segment). Returns slug, source_id, type, title, source_path and updated_at per page, t